            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLFrame">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZCLFrame</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> contains a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLHeader">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZCLHeader</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>, and a
    payload. It must used when invoking a command.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLHeader">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZCLHeader</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> describes the header of a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLFrame">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZCLFrame</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The transaction id of each <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLHeader">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZCLHeader</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> must
    be managed by the base driver.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Only getters (not setters) are shared by client applications, the
    base driver and endpoint implementations. Therefore only getters are
    specified.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d1850e1565">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">ZigBee Group</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>149.28</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>ZigBee Group</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
               <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZigBeeGroup</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> enables group management (that is, it provides
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup.joinGroup-String-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">joinGroup(String)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup.leaveGroup-String-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">leaveGroup(String)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> methods).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The creation of groups is made through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.createGroupService-int-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">createGroupService(int)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A ZigBeeGroup service should be registered with the following
    property:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d1850e1579">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d1850e1580">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup.ID">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">ID</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – (zigbee.group.id/Integer) The 16-bit group
        address of the device.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">And, the following <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZigBeeEndpoint</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>
    properties:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d1850e1588">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d1850e1589">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint.DEVICE_CATEGORY">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">DEVICE_CATEGORY</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d1850e1592">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint.INPUT_CLUSTERS">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">INPUT_CLUSTERS</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d1850e1595">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint.HOST_PID">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">HOST_PID</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ZigBeeGroup</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> service enables the ZigBee groupcasting of command
    invocation thanks to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup.groupcast-int-ZCLFrame-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">groupcast(int,ZCLFrame)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeGroup.groupcast-int-ZCLFrame-String-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">groupcast(int,ZCLFrame,String)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> methods. A groupcast message is received by the
    endpoints that are members of the targeted group.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d1850e1606">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">ZigBee Networking</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>149.29</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>ZigBee Networking</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1608">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.29.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Logical node type</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The ZigBee specification defines three types of ZigBee nodes on
      the network:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d1850e1611">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1612">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>ZigBee Coordinator (ZC) – The most capable device, the
          coordinator forms the root of the network. There is exactly one
          ZigBee coordinator in every network. It is able to store information
          about the network, to act as the Trust Center and repository for
          security keys. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.COORDINATOR">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">COORDINATOR</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> represents the ZigBee coordinator.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1617">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>ZigBee Router (ZR) – A router is capable of extending a ZigBee
          network by routing data from other ZigBee devices. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.ROUTER">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">ROUTER</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> represents a ZigBee router.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1622">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>ZigBee End Device (ZED) – An end device contains just enough
          functionality to talk to the parent node (either the coordinator or
          a router); it cannot relay data from other devices. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.ZED">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">ZED</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> represents a ZigBee end device.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Every discovered <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeNode</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> on
      the network has a logical node type returned by calling the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.descriptors.ZigBeeNodeDescriptor.getLogicalType--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getLogicalType()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method on the node's <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.descriptors.ZigBeeNodeDescriptor">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeNodeDescriptor</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1635">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.29.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Network selection</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The base driver provides a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      object for every available ZigBee local host. A ZigBee local host can
      represent a ZigBee chip on a USB dongle, a ZigBee built-in chip or a
      ZigBee Gateway Device (see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="service.zigbee-ref-zigbee-gateway">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[7] <fo:inline font-style="italic">ZigBee Gateway</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>). This object must be
      registered as a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> service. The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      interface has methods to start and stop the host, to store the
      networking configuration information (channel, channel mask, logical
      type, PAN ID, Extended PAN ID, security level, network key), and to open
      the network for devices to join it (<fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.permitJoin-short-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">permitJoin(short)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>).</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> also enables the broadcast of ZCL commands on a
      ZigBee network thanks to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.broadcast-int-ZCLFrame-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">broadcast(int,ZCLFrame)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.broadcast-int-ZCLFrame-String-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">broadcast(int,ZCLFrame,String)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> methods. Broadcasting enables the sending of a
      ZCL command to all clusters identified with an identifier of all
      endpoints available on the nodes of a ZigBee network within a number of
      hops defined by the broadcast radius of the coordinator (see the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.getBroadcastRadius--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getBroadcastRadius()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.setBroadcastRadius-short-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">setBroadcastRadius(short)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> methods).</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">In ZigBee networks, the coordinator must select a PAN identifier
      and a channel to start a network. After that, it behaves essentially
      like a router. The coordinator and routers can allow other devices to
      join the network and route data.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">After an end device joins a router or coordinator, it is able to
      transmit or receive data through that router or coordinator. The router
      or coordinator that allowed an end device to join becomes the parent of
      the end device. Since the end device can sleep, the parent must be able
      to buffer or retain incoming data packets targeting the end device until
      the end device is able to wake up and receive the data.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1662">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.29.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Network coordination</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> is configured as the network coordinator, the
      <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.descriptors.ZigBeeNodeDescriptor.getLogicalType--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getLogicalType()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method on the node's <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.descriptors.ZigBeeNodeDescriptor">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeNodeDescriptor</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> MUST return <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.COORDINATOR">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">COORDINATOR</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      object will then be able to use the following operations for managing
      the network:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d1850e1676">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1677">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.updateNetworkChannel-byte-">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">updateNetworkChannel(byte)</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - Updates the network channel.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1681">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.setChannelMask-int-">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">setChannelMask(int)</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - Sets a new configured channel mask.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d1850e1685">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.refreshNetwork--">
                                 <fo:inline color="blue"
                                            font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                            hyphenate="false">refreshNetwork()</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> – Requests the base driver to launch new
          discovery requests and refresh devices service registration
          according to current devices availability. This method is made
          mandatory since ZigBee specification allows devices not to notify
          the network when they leave it.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1689">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.29.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Networking considerations</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Network Address is a 16-bit address that is assigned by the
      coordinator when a node has joined a network and that must be unique for
      a given network in order for the node to be identified uniquely. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeNode</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      provides <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.getNetworkAddress--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getNetworkAddress()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.getIEEEAddress--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getIEEEAddress()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> which returns device network address and device
      IEEE MAC address.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d1850e1699">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Security</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>149.30</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Security</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1701">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.30.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Security management</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">ZigBee security is based on a 128-bit algorithm built on the
      security model provided by IEEE 802.15.4. ZigBee specification which
      defines the Trust Center.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Trust Center is the device trusted by devices within a network
      to distribute keys for the purpose of network and end-to-end application
      configuration management. All members of the network shall recognize
      exactly one Trust Center, and there shall be exactly one Trust Center in
      each secure network.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The security of a network of ZigBee devices is based on link keys
      and a network key. Unicast communication between entities is secured by
      means of a 128-bit link key shared by two devices, one of those is
      normally the Trust Center. Broadcast communications are secured by means
      of a 128-bit network key shared among all devices in the network. The
      master key is only used as an initial shared secret between two devices
      when they perform the Key Establishment to generate Link Keys.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Security configuration is provided by the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.getSecurityLevel--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getSecurityLevel()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method returning whether the security mode is
      activated or not on the ZigBee network.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeHost</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> with a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode.COORDINATOR">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">COORDINATOR</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> logical node type will acts as a the Trust
      Center according to the ZigBee specification. It can also be any other
      device on the network. The Trust Center stores all the shared network
      keys. The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeHost.getPreconfiguredLinkKey--">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getPreconfiguredLinkKey()</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method returns the network master key.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1718">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>149.30.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Conditional permission</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When a bundle registers a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">ZigBeeEndpoint</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      OSGi service, then the base driver exposes this endpoint on the outside
      ZigBee network and this endpoint has the ability to communicate with the
      other network devices. The base driver also provides an equivalent
      behavior when discovering a ZigBee endpoint from the outside network and
      exposing it as an OSGi Service in the OSGi Framework service registry.
      It is therefore recommended that
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[ZigBeeHost|ZigBeeEndpoint|ZCLEventListener,
      REGISTER|GET]</fo:inline> be used sparingly and only for trusted
      bundles.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.zigbee">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">org.osgi.service.zigbee</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>149.31</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>org.osgi.service.zigbee<fo:inline id="org.osgi.service.zigbee-version"/>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
Device Service Specification for ZigBee Technology.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 This is the main package of this specification. It defines the interfaces
 that models the ZigBee concepts, like the ZigBee node and the ZigBee
 endpoint.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Each time a new ZigBee node is discovered, the driver will register a
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeNode} service and then one 
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint} service for
 each ZigBee endpoint discovered on the node.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint} interface provides the
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZigBeeEndpoint#getServerCluster(int)} method 
 to get an  interface reference to a ZCLCluster object.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLCluster} interface contains methods that directly maps to the ZCL
 profile-wide commands, like Read Attributes and Write Attributes, and allow
 the developer to forge its own commands and send them through the invoke()
 methods.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 ZCL Attribute reportings are configured, registering a
 {@link org.osgi.service.zigbee.ZCLEventListener}, provided that this service 
 is registered with the right service properties.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 In addition to ZCL frames, the current specification allows also to send ZDP
 frames. Broadcasting and endpoint broadcasting is also supported for ZCL
 frames.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Bundles wishing to use this package must list the package in the
 Import-Package header of the bundle's manifest. This package has two types of
 users: the consumers that use the API in this package and the providers that
 implement the API in this package.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for consumers using the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.zigbee; version="[1.0,2.0)"}
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for providers implementing the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.zigbee; version="[1.0,1.1)"}</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d1850e1746">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
